If LVZ is supported in the future, there will be a two-level page table
walk. This patch replaces address_space_ldq_le with the cpu_ldq_le_xxx API
for page table entry loading. The latter API uses the QEMU CPU TLB and
automatically triggers the second-level page table walk. It can also
generate a page fault exception if the second-level page table walk fails.

Bibo Mao (3):
  target/loongarch: Replace address_space_ldq_le() ->
    cpu_ldq_le_data_ra()
  target/loongarch: Use input parameter mmu_idx rather than current mode
  target/loongarch: Replace address_space_ldq_le -> cpu_ldq_le_mmuidx_ra
    in loongarch_ptw

